# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) wants to check
# files out as CRLF while the tooling here writes LF. Generated files, the
# Paraglide output in particular, then show up as permanently modified even
# though their content is byte-identical to the index.
#
# The app is built and run inside Linux containers, so LF everywhere is also
# what production expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings (they run inside Linux containers).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes, never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.sqlite binary
